## Details worth raising

| Detail | Why |
|--------|-----|
| Three states: light, dark, **system** | "Follow system" is a real user preference, not the absence of one |
| `color-scheme: light dark` in CSS | Makes native scrollbars and form controls match |
| Disable transitions during the switch | Otherwise every element animates at once and it looks like a glitch |
| `<meta name="theme-color">` | Colours the mobile browser chrome |
| Test contrast in both themes | Dark mode contrast failures are extremely common |

## URL as the source of truth

```jsx
function ProductSearch() {
  const [searchParams, setSearchParams] = useSearchParams();

  // Derived from the URL — never duplicated into state
  const query = searchParams.get('q') ?? '';
  const category = searchParams.get('category') ?? 'all';
  const sort = searchParams.get('sort') ?? 'relevance';
  const page = Number(searchParams.get('page') ?? 1);

  const updateParams = useCallback((patch, { replace = false } = {}) => {
    setSearchParams((prev) => {
      const next = new URLSearchParams(prev);

      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(patch)) {
        if (value == null || value === '' || value === 'all') {
          next.delete(key);              // keep the URL clean
        } else {
          next.set(key, String(value));
        }
      }

      if (!('page' in patch)) next.delete('page');   // any filter change resets pagination
      return next;
    }, { replace });
  }, [setSearchParams]);

  return (
    <>
      <SearchInput value={query} onChange={(q) => updateParams({ q }, { replace: true })} />

      <select value={category} onChange={(e) => updateParams({ category: e.target.value })}>
        …
      </select>

      <Results query={query} category={category} sort={sort} page={page} />
    </>
  );
}
```

